                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS State College PA",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 27 at 3:07PM EDT until August 28 at 2:00AM EDT by NWS State College PA",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of central Pennsylvania, including the following\ncounties, Lancaster, Lebanon and Schuylkill.\n\n* WHEN...Until 2 AM EDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nCreeks and streams may rise out of their banks. Flooding may occur\nin poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Heavy thunderstorm downpours with rainfall rates of 1 to 2 inches\nper hour could produce scattered areas of flash flooding late\nthis afternoon into the first half of tonight.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Please monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action should\nFlash Flood Warnings be issued.",
